    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test passing, plus a clean compile which exercises the OpenAPI regeneration and MapStruct mapping).\n\n## What I did\n\n`riskFlag` is now a read-only boolean on the owner response, `true` when **any** of the three conditions hold, else `false`. I implemented it the same way the codebase computes its other derived fields (`ownerSegment`, `contactPreference`, \u2026): as a mapper expression over already-persisted owner state \u2014 so it needs no new DB column or pipeline step, and `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it by reloading the owner.\n\nThe three conditions map to existing infrastructure:\n- **Possible duplicate** \u2192 the persisted `possibleDuplicate` flag (set by `DetectPossibleDuplicate`).\n- **City over soft capacity** \u2192 the persisted `capacityWarning` flag (the 40\u201349 warning band set by `FlagCityCapacityWarning`; hard capacity at 50 is already a create-time rejection).\n- **Disposable-adjacent email domain** \u2192 a new, softer check (exact disposable domains are already rejected at create with a 400, so they never reach here). \"Adjacent\" means a subdomain of a blocked provider (`mail.mailinator.com`) or a same-brand domain on a different TLD (`mailinator.net`, `tempmail.io`), matched by shared second-level label.\n\nFiles changed:\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `riskFlag` schema property (regenerates into `OwnerDto`).\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 added the `riskFlag` mapping expression.\n- New `RiskFlag.java` \u2014 combines the three conditions.\n- New `DisposableEmailDomains.java` \u2014 single source of truth for the blocklist, exposing both the exact-`isBlocked` and the softer `isDisposableAdjacent` checks.\n- `RejectDisposableEmailDomain.java` \u2014 refactored to reuse that shared blocklist (behavior unchanged) so the reject rule and the risk signal can't drift apart.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreRiskFlagFalseNormally` passes (a fully-unique owner with no email trips none of the conditions \u2192 `false`), and the full suite builds and runs green.",
